                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "39218108",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561197976278037",
                            "num_reviews": 50,
                            "playtime_forever": 201,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 201,
                            "last_played": 1515538579
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Eh, game is okay.  It's a bit fun but it's also frustrating, typical of anything with permadeath.  Hard to maintain any sort of army long enough to build up strong units once the difficulty gets to a certain level.  The difficulty rises pretty quickly and becomes a war of attrition as the gold and experience earnings don't seem to be rising at the same speed as the difficulty.  Also, just in case you get comfortable and start making progress, the game will also send enemy armies to capture your castle, so you'll also have to split your gold for defenses.  Granted, you do get a town portal, that won't help you if you get caught in a battle right when an enemy is heading to your castle.\n\nGame plays a bit like Might and Magic/King's Bounty but in real time with no tactical squares/hexagons and randomly generated maps.  Some thought is also needed as far as whether or not you will rush through acts or if you will try to build up your hero/army.  Each playthrough feels like a bit of a puzzle due to the RNG.\n \nThere seems to be a bug that prevents you from picking up item chests sometimes, which has the possibility of leaving you 1 good item behind.\n\nI'll recommend it, albeit with a little hesitation.  The cheeky way the game tries to defeat you becomes obnoxious since there is that layer of RNG on top of it.",
                        "timestamp_created": 1515536213,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1515538507,
                        "voted_up": true,
                        "votes_up": 16,
                        "votes_funny": 0,
                        "weighted_vote_score": 0.6816759705543518,
                        "comment_count": 1,
                        "steam_purchase": true,
                        "received_for_free": false,
                        "written_during_early_access": false,
                        "developer_response": "Thanks for the honest review Dbrn! I totally get how the challenge can feel relentless, especially with permadeath in the mix. Balancing risk and resource management is a big part of Sky Is Arrows, but I hear you on the difficulty ramp—it's something that always needs fine-tuning. Your point about gold and experience scaling is a good one, and I'll take another look at how that plays out in longer runs.\n\nAlso, thanks for flagging the item chest bug! That has been resolved at this point-- and if somehow it happens you can enter a battle if one remains on the map, then return to the chest.\n\nGlad you still found some fun in the experience, and I appreciate you giving the game a shot (and a recommendation!). Please look for the Ebonhare Visage Item Chest on Feb 24th that comes along with version 11.1",
                        "timestamp_dev_responded": 1738901505,
                        "primarily_steam_deck": false,
                        "refunded": false
                    }
                ],
